/*
   Localizable.strings (العربية)
   AS Music

   SwiftUI's Text("…") takes a LocalizedStringKey, so the English string in the
   source doubles as the lookup key and no code had to change to add this file.

   Translation notes:
   * Modern Standard Arabic, and deliberately not word-for-word. Interface
     Arabic should read like an app, not like a translated manual: "تشغيل"
     (play) rather than a literal rendering, "المكتبة" for Library, and so on.
   * Verbs are imperatives for buttons ("احفظ", "احذف"), verbal nouns for
     titles and section headers ("الإعدادات", "التنزيلات").
   * Technical terms that Arabic speakers actually use in Latin script are kept
     that way (Wi-Fi, EQ, AI, MP3) — transliterating them reads as noise.
   * The app's own coined names (Magic DL, Smart Radio) are translated where a
     natural Arabic equivalent exists and left alone where it does not.
*/

